{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And behold, seven other cows.</b> He called them 'other' because it is said (Psalms 147:14), ״הַשָּׂם גְּבוּלֵךְ שָׁלוֹם חֵלֶב חִטִּים יַשְׂבִּיעֵךְ״ — and when the measure of a Kad is full, one knocks and adversity comes (Bava Metzi'a 59a) — and each one becomes 'other' to his fellow; their hearts are divided and they are not as one. And for this reason, regarding the good ears of grain it says ״עוֹלוֹת בְּקָנֶה אֶחָד,״ indicating unity, and by implication it is understood that among the bad ones there is no unity. And so too regarding the cows He mentioned ״אֲחֵרוֹת״ for the bad ones, and by implication it is understood that among the good ones they are not 'other' but unified.\nAnother matter: therefore He called them ״אֲחֵרוֹת״ because each and every year its curse was greater than that of its fellow, for the famine grows and intensifies; therefore each year was like a different year, but the years of plenty were all equal in goodness.\nAnother matter: because they are days of distress, therefore they appeared as many days; but the good years were as a few days, in love, amidst delights." "<b>And they stood beside the cows.</b> This indicates that the cows were so evil and emaciated that they had scarcely any strength to stand on their legs; and that they did stand was only because they were beside the good cows, which supported them. And this is a sign that the creatures would have had no survival and no standing in the years of famine were it not for their being beside the good years adjacent to them — therefore there was a stay and a support for the years of famine from the years of plenty, as it is written (Genesis 41:20), ״וַתֹּאכַלְנָה הַפָּרוֹת הָרָעוֹת״ — to hint that in the years of famine they would consume from the produce of the years of plenty."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:32:52.819964364Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}